{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788469514575,"sessionID":"ses_f96ee63ceffebQ0LD64zWsaHwP","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_9a12433d7d104157b1d814ec","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-param-destructure-build/src/ast.rs","oldString":"#[derive(Debug)]\npub struct Param {\n    pub name: String,\n    pub ty: TypeExpr,\n    pub span: Span,\n}","newString":"/// What a parameter's left side binds: either one name or a record destructured the way a match\n/// arm's brace pattern destructures one. The type annotation stays fully explicit either way.\n#[derive(Debug)]\npub enum ParamShape {\n    /// `name` in `fn f(name: T) -> R`.\n    Name(String, Span),\n    /// `{a, b, ..}` in `fn f({a, b}: T) -> R`, binding each named field of the record `T`.\n    Fields(FieldsPattern),\n}\n\nimpl ParamShape {\n    pub fn span(&self) -> Span {\n        match self {\n            ParamShape::Name(_, span) => *span,\n            ParamShape::Fields(f) => f.span,\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n#[derive(Debug)]\npub struct Param {\n    pub shape: ParamShape,\n    pub ty: TypeExpr,\n    pub span: Span,\n}"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-param-destructure-build/src/ast.rs\n===================================================================\n--- /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-param-destructure-build/src/ast.rs\n+++ /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-param-destructure-build/src/ast.rs\n@@ -118,11 +118,30 @@\n         }\n     }\n }\n \n+/// What a parameter's left side binds: either one name or a record destructured the way a match\n+/// arm's brace pattern destructures one. The type annotation stays fully explicit either way.\n #[derive(Debug)]\n+pub enum ParamShape {\n+    /// `name` in `fn f(name: T) -> R`.\n+    Name(String, Span),\n+    /// `{a, b, ..}` in `fn f({a, b}: T) -> R`, binding each named field of the record `T`.\n+    Fields(FieldsPattern),\n+}\n+\n+impl ParamShape {\n+    pub fn span(&self) -> Span {\n+        match self {\n+            ParamShape::Name(_, span) => *span,\n+            ParamShape::Fields(f) => f.span,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Debug)]\n pub struct Param {\n-    pub name: String,\n+    pub shape: ParamShape,\n     pub ty: TypeExpr,\n     pub span: Span,\n }\n \n","filediff":{"file":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-param-destructure-build/src/ast.rs","patch":"Index: /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-param-destructure-build/src/ast.rs\n===================================================================\n--- /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-param-destructure-build/src/ast.rs\n+++ /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-param-destructure-build/src/ast.rs\n@@ -118,11 +118,30 @@\n         }\n     }\n }\n \n+/// What a parameter's left side binds: either one name or a record destructured the way a match\n+/// arm's brace pattern destructures one. The type annotation stays fully explicit either way.\n #[derive(Debug)]\n+pub enum ParamShape {\n+    /// `name` in `fn f(name: T) -> R`.\n+    Name(String, Span),\n+    /// `{a, b, ..}` in `fn f({a, b}: T) -> R`, binding each named field of the record `T`.\n+    Fields(FieldsPattern),\n+}\n+\n+impl ParamShape {\n+    pub fn span(&self) -> Span {\n+        match self {\n+            ParamShape::Name(_, span) => *span,\n+            ParamShape::Fields(f) => f.span,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Debug)]\n pub struct Param {\n-    pub name: String,\n+    pub shape: ParamShape,\n     pub ty: TypeExpr,\n     pub span: Span,\n }\n \n","additions":20,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"src/ast.rs","time":{"start":1788469514571,"end":1788469514574}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now let me make the AST change. I'll add `ParamShape` enum and change `Param`. Let me write the edit.\